{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>The end of the matter.</b> I have already made you hear everything, or: you have heard every dispute of the sages. Do this: fear Elohim." "<b>For this is the whole of man.</b> It refers back to the preceding matter, which is that man in his life and in his death is vanity, and its meaning is: for this is the lot of all man. Or: for this is the essence of all man, and it refers back to fear of HaShem, the honored and awesome One."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:29:23.997782363Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}